      "content": "Your symptoms are a classic sign of Deep Vein Thrombosis (DVT), which is a life-threatening blood clot that requires immediate medical attention, not just water and sleep. You must stop walking and go to the ER immediately to get an ultrasound, as waiting could lead to a fatal pulmonary embolism. Do not try to \"sleep it off\" or self-medicate; your shallow breathing and calf pain are critical red flags that demand professional intervention right now.",
